      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "Note"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "Edit the Character Creator on the left, then queue the workflow.\n\nInstalled Qwen Image 2.1 INT8 model + Qwen3-VL encoder + Qwen 2.1 VAE. Uses the existing local workflow settings: 25 steps, CFG 1, Euler/simple, 1024 square.\n\nControlNets are disabled by default. To use compatible weights, add Character ControlNet Entry nodes, connect each loaded model and preprocessed hint, enable the creator's ControlNet selector, and connect entries to its growing slots. The stack is already routed through Apply Character ControlNets.\n\nText encoding and ControlNet application use separate nodes.\n\nThe creator negative_prompt output is connected to negative text encoding. SD/SDXL generate concise style/crop-aware negatives; Qwen currently outputs an empty negative. Disconnect this link to enter your own negative text."
      ],
      "title": "Start here / ControlNet wiring"
    }
